&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;The role:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;Nebius is building the cloud infrastructure that will power the next generation of Physical AI—robotics, autonomous systems, simulation, and embodied intelligence operating in the real world. As a European-headquartered AI infrastructure company, EMEA is a strategic home market for Nebius and one of the most consequential regions in the global Physical AI buildout—from UK autonomy and foundation-model players, to German humanoid and industrial robotics, to Swiss legged-robotics and Israeli/Nordic frontier startups, to the EU&#39;s rapidly accelerating defence and dual-use AI ecosystem.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;The Principal, EMEA GTM – Physical AI owns our GTM motion across EMEA: a regional sales overlay role built to drive repeatable revenue within our first and most important segment—Physical AI natives based in or operating across Europe, the Middle East, and Africa. This is not a generalist regional AE seat. It is a domain-led, EMEA-anchored pipeline generator and deal accelerator designed to create leverage: tighter narratives, sharper use-case framing, and category assets that the EMEA field can run independently.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;You will open strategic, executive-level accounts across the EMEA Physical AI ecosystem, generate qualified pipeline, and personally lead engagement across our EMEA Top 25 target list. On top-tier deals, you will partner directly with EMEA Account Executives, regional sales leadership, and the Physical AI Field CTO team to shape the opportunity early, act as executive sponsor, and accelerate time-to-close. In parallel, you will turn what you learn in-region into repeatable motions—subsegment theses, playbooks, and enablement—tailored to the EMEA buyer, the regulatory environment (EU AI Act, GDPR, data sovereignty), and the region&#39;s multi-country go-to-market complexity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;This is a definitive “zero-to-one” opportunity to build the EMEA commercial foundation for a new cloud category from the ground up, in a region where Nebius has structural home-market advantage. You are welcome to work remotely from within EMEA, with strong preference for London or Munich; Paris or Amsterdam are also viable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EMEA Pipeline Generation &amp;amp; Account Ownership:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Generate qualified, industry-sourced pipeline and open strategic, executive-level accounts within the EMEA Physical AI ecosystem—autonomous vehicles, humanoid and industrial robotics, foundation-model and world-model builders, industrial computer vision, and the OEM/Tier-1 cohort investing in Physical AI in Germany, France, Sweden, and Italy. Personally own engagement for our EMEA Top 25 target list and ensure each account has a clear engagement plan and is actively progressing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal Acceleration with the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EMEA Field:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Frame use cases and shape solution direction in the early stages of a deal. Partner directly with EMEA AEs, regional GMs, and the Field CTO on top-tier accounts to accelerate closure, acting as the executive sponsor and regional domain authority. Your involvement is the difference between a stalled deal and a closed one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EMEA Lighthouse Account Execution:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Identify and secure the most innovative companies across EMEA&#39;s AI-native Physical AI segments—autonomy, humanoid robotics, foundation/world-model builders, simulation-first startups, defense and dual-use—converting them into flagship customer wins that validate our platform, establish category credibility in-region, and create reference gravity for the rest of EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Subsegment Theses &amp;amp; Category Building (EMEA Lens):&lt;/strong&gt; Define EMEA-specific subsegment theses and extract cross-account insights to establish repeatable deal patterns. Identify which European customer profiles convert fastest, which use cases generate the highest consumption, which objections appear most frequently (sovereignty, AI Act compliance, data residency, EU-based support), and which regional GTM motions actually work. Operationalize those learnings into scalable sales plays the EMEA field can run.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EMEA Sales Playbook Development:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Codify market learnings into a comprehensive “EMEA Physical AI Playbook.” Develop battle cards, positioning guides, objection-handling frameworks, and competitive intelligence materials specific to the EMEA buyer. Deliver formalized, documented sales motions that the broader EMEA field team—across the UK, DACH, France, Benelux, Nordics, Southern Europe, the Middle East, and Israel—can execute independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Field Enablement:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as a force multiplier for the EMEA sales organization. Run internal enablement sessions and training for EMEA Sales, SAs, and Marketing on Physical AI positioning, target personas, regional regulatory framing (EU AI Act, GDPR, sovereignty), and use-case framing. Publish case studies and reference stories from EMEA lighthouse wins to arm the broader regional team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Revenue Conversion in Region:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the long-term revenue trajectory of the Physical AI domain in EMEA, ensuring that early lighthouse technical wins translate into high-volume compute consumption as customers scale their training, simulation, and inference workloads on Nebius infrastructure—and that EMEA contributes its full share of the Physical AI revenue target.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;E&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MEA Market Intelligence &amp;amp; Competitive Positioning:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain a real-time understanding of the EMEA Physical AI competitive landscape. Track where other cloud providers are winning or losing within our target segments. Feed competitive intelligence into sales assets and deal strategy. Position Nebius&#39;s European-headquartered, sovereignty-friendly posture as a structural advantage where it matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Ecosystem Evangelism:&lt;/strong&gt; Evangelize our capabilities at EMEA-relevant industry events (e.g., Hannover Messe, Automatica, European Robotics Forum, VivaTech, AI Summit London, Web Summit, Slush, and EMEA editions of ICRA/IROS/CoRL when applicable) and customer executive briefings—positioning Nebius as the infrastructure of choice for Physical AI workloads built and deployed in Europe and across the broader EMEA region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;We expect you to have:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7+ years &lt;/strong&gt;of experience in sales overlay, GTM strategy, or domain-specialist selling within Cloud, AI Infrastructure, or High-Performance Computing—with a meaningful portion of that experience focused on EMEA customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EMEA Operating Fluency: &lt;/strong&gt;Deep familiarity with how to sell across the UK, DACH, France, Benelux, Nordics, Southern Europe, the Middle East, and Israel. You understand that EMEA is not one market and you have a point of view on which subregions to lead with for a category like Physical AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven Pipeline Generation: &lt;/strong&gt;Demonstrated track record of personally sourcing and generating qualified pipeline across EMEA through outbound prospecting, industry relationships, and strategic account engagement at the executive level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal Acceleration DNA: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience partnering with Account Executives across multiple EMEA countries to accelerate complex enterprise and startup deals. You know how to frame a use case, position value, and act as an executive sponsor to drive closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Playbook Builder: &lt;/strong&gt;You have built GTM motions from scratch before—segmenting a market, defining the pitch, creating the sales plays, and training a broader regional team to execute. Bonus if you have done it specifically for EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep Domain Fluency: &lt;/strong&gt;You speak the language of the builders. You understand the difference between model training, simulation, synthetic data generation, and inference workloads. You know the key players—startups and incumbents—across the modern Physical AI stack, with strong recall of the European cohort specifically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory &amp;amp; Sovereignty Awareness: &lt;/strong&gt;Working knowledge of the EU AI Act, GDPR, data-residency expectations, and the sovereign-cloud conversation in Europe. You can speak credibly with customers for whom these are first-order procurement considerations rather than afterthoughts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enablement Mindset: &lt;/strong&gt;You enjoy teaching and scaling knowledge. You can take complex technical wins and distill them into simple, repeatable sales motions for a broader EMEA team that lacks your domain depth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Orchestration: &lt;/strong&gt;Proven track record of working across Sales, SAs, Marketing, and Product Marketing—often across multiple EMEA countries and time zones—to align distinct teams behind a unified GTM execution plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Startup &amp;amp; AI-Native Fluency: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience working with (or selling to) high-growth, venture-backed European startups. You understand the urgency, the technical depth, and the rapid decision-making of this customer base, as well as how European founders and CTOs evaluate infrastructure differently from their US counterparts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication: &lt;/strong&gt;Strong executive presence and communication skills, capable of holding your own with VC-backed founders, CTOs, and senior technical decision-makers across EMEA. Additional European languages (German, French) are a plus, not a requirement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfort in Ambiguity: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience operating in fast-moving environments where the sales motion is not yet fully defined and requires real-time iteration and pattern recognition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;Why Nebius:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Ownership: &lt;/strong&gt;You are not inheriting a quota on an existing product line in an existing region; you are building the EMEA revenue engine for an entirely new category of cloud infrastructure, in our strategic home market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Category Definition: &lt;/strong&gt;Define the EMEA playbook that the rest of the company will use to sell Physical AI in the region for years to come.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontier Technology: &lt;/strong&gt;Work at the bleeding edge of embodied intelligence, engaging with the companies defining the future of robotics, autonomy, and the physical world—right at the center of Europe&#39;s accelerating AI buildout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structural Advantage: &lt;/strong&gt;Nebius is European-headquartered. Sovereignty, EU data residency, and regulatory alignment are real selling points—not retrofits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High Leverage: &lt;/strong&gt;Focus on the top 10% of transformative EMEA customers that drive the next 90% of growth within this segment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission: &lt;/strong&gt;Help define how intelligence moves from the data center into the physical world—starting from Europe. &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-GH1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
