&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Service Designer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; London (Hybrid) | &lt;strong&gt;Practice Area:&lt;/strong&gt; Product &amp;amp; Experience | &lt;strong&gt;Type:&lt;/strong&gt; Permanent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design with impact. Lead with empathy. Transform experiences.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Capco is looking for a Senior Service Designer to help create customer-centric products and services that drive meaningful change in financial services and energy. You’ll work on complex transformation programmes addressing today’s most relevant challenges, from advancing inclusive design in high-street banking to helping global organisations adopt customer-driven operating models. You&#39;ll also help clients identify where AI-enabled capabilities can enhance customer experiences and service delivery in a responsible and user-centred way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate senior-level workshops and lead discovery activities to define experience design strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate user needs into concepts, service blueprints, and artefacts that align business strategy with user needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to incorporate AI-enabled capabilities, such as personalisation or automation, into service concepts where they enhance customer and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the design of customer journey management approaches, including AI-enabled insight where appropriate to improve service performance and decision-making&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
